    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** lineup for July 12, 2026, is headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, who leads the squad with an elite 81.88 efficiency score. His favorable park factors and the +14% platoon edge against Lugo make him our primary offensive anchor. Joining him in the elite tier are **Jacob Wilson** (71.63) and **Andy Pages** (71.40), both of whom capitalize on high-upside matchups against pitchers with xERAs above 4.80. **Kyle Tucker** (75.35) remains a set-and-forget play, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (70.23) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (69.55) provide significant run-production potential, with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefiting immensely from a soft matchup against M\u00e1rquez (5.58 xERA).\n\nWe are aggressively exploiting speed and delivery metrics to chase stolen bases today. **Josh Lowe** (62.32) and **Jackson Merrill** (63.99) are both projected for efficient performances, bolstered by the \"slow delivery\" factor against their respective opposing pitchers, which maximizes our stolen base probability. **Sam Antonacci** (65.67) and **Heliot Ramos** (63.48) also round out a deep starting nine that maintains high efficiency across all slots. Our most difficult decision on the bench was **Brayan Rocchio** (56.28), who performed well in his analysis but ultimately yielded to the higher projected efficiency of our starting middle infielders. **Miguel Vargas** (56.21) also drew consideration due to his elite 0.403 xwOBA, but he failed to clear the threshold for this specific matchup profile.\n\nInvestors should monitor the weather closely, particularly for **Drake Baldwin** (50.66), as wind-in conditions have slightly tempered his base projection. While our core remains strong, we have successfully benched **Denzer Guzman** (38.35) and **Dominic Smith** (43.23) to preserve our daily game caps, as both failed to reach the threshold for an \"Elite\" or \"Strong\" start. With **Liam Hicks** (43.11) tasked with a challenging matchup against the lefty Cantillo, we are prioritizing the high-upside ceiling of our core stars to maximize our 5x5 category output.",
